      "message": "Looks like Colin is OOO, so asking @dwillemsen...\n\nDan, do you know why `genrule` doesn\u0027t support any kind of way to do what I want to do -- define the base `cmd` in a genrule_defaults and slightly modify it in actual inheriting rules.\n\nFor example, it\u0027d be cool if genrule supported arguments like below, so I could move the cmd to defaults:\n\n```\ncmd: \"cp $(cp_arg) ...\"\n\nargs: {\n   cp_arg: \"-p\",\n}\n```\n\nThough, of course, I don\u0027t think you can use arbitrary property names. Then maybe we could pre-define 10 or so arguments:\n```\ncmd: \"cp $(arg1) ...\"\n\nargs: {\n   arg1: \"-p\",\n}\n```\n\nFor now though, I just want to append extra arguments to `cmd`, so currently I ended up with this CL.\n\nIs there any reason we shouldn\u0027t do it? (Other than being a little hacky.)",
